# Implementation Plan - SIMAD oLearn Design Package

This plan outlines the structure and content generation strategy for the SIMAD oLearn Distance Learning Platform design specifications.

## Goal Description
To design a comprehensive, secure, and scalable distance learning platform ("SIMAD oLearn") that supports end-to-end teaching, learning, and high-stakes integrity-focused examinations. The output will be a set of detailed professional specification documents.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Branding & Originality**: All content will be original and strictly branded "SIMAD oLearn".
> **Academic Integrity**: Special focus on the "Exam Shield" and non-bypassable proctoring features.
> **Format**: The deliverables will be organized into structured Markdown documents found in the `design_specs/` directory for easy export and reading.

## Proposed Deliverables Structure

I will generate the following detailed files in `design_specs/`:

#### [NEW] internal/design_specs/01_PRD_and_Scope.md
*   **Vision & Goals**
*   **Personas & Use Cases**
*   **Requirements (FR/NFR)**
*   **Core Feature Scope** (LMS, Assessment, Exam Shield, Services, Analytics)

#### [NEW] internal/design_specs/02_Roles_and_Processes.md
*   **Roles & Permissions Matrix**
*   **End-to-End Work Process Maps** (Course Lifecycle, Exam Lifecycle, Misconduct, etc.)

#### [NEW] internal/design_specs/03_Architecture_and_Roadmap.md
*   **High-Level System Architecture**
*   **Security, Privacy, Compliance**
*   **Phased Roadmap**

## Verification Plan
### Manual Verification
*   **Constraint Check**: Verify "SIMAD oLearn" branding is used consistently.
*   **Completeness Check**: Ensure all sections from the user prompt are present.
*   **Integrity Check**: Ensure no "cheating instructions" are present, only prevention/detection measures.
*   **Flow Consistency**: Verify that process maps align with the feature definitions.
